conv.cat — licensing overview
Copyright (c) 2026 tachsin

This repository is licensed under TWO different licences, depending on which
directory the code lives in. This file is a map, not a licence: nothing here
grants or restricts any right on its own. The authoritative terms are the
`LICENSE` file inside each directory listed below.

================================================================================
MIT — the reusable engine and libraries
================================================================================

  crates/conv-core       crates/conv-core/LICENSE
  crates/conv-wasm       crates/conv-wasm/LICENSE
  packages/engine        packages/engine/LICENSE
  packages/media         packages/media/LICENSE
  packages/data          packages/data/LICENSE

You may use these inside your own software, including closed-source and
commercial software, under the terms of the MIT licence.

================================================================================
AGPL-3.0-only — the applications
================================================================================

  apps/web               apps/web/LICENSE
  apps/desktop           apps/desktop/LICENSE

These are the conv.cat applications themselves. Under the GNU Affero General
Public License v3.0 (only, not "or later"), if you run a modified version of
these applications and let other people use it over a network, you must offer
those users the complete corresponding source of your modified version.

================================================================================
Anything else in this repository
================================================================================

Files outside the directories listed above — the repository root, `docs/`, and
`.github/` — are supporting material (configuration, documentation, CI). They
are made available under the MIT licence, with one exception: the conv.cat
brand, described below, is not licensed at all.

================================================================================
Trademark and brand — NOT covered by either licence
================================================================================

The licences above cover source code. They do not grant any right to the
conv.cat name, the conv.cat domain, or the conv.cat logo and mascot. A fork may
use, modify and redistribute the code; it may not present itself as conv.cat.
See the "Trademark" section of README.md.

================================================================================
Third-party dependencies
================================================================================

Dependencies pulled in by Cargo and pnpm carry their own licences, which are
unaffected by this file.
